msgid ""
"Require PKCE on the authorization endpoint for this app (RFC 7636 / 9700). "
"Default: True. Pass --no-pkce-required for known-incompatible legacy clients."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mint a fresh RSA private key for JWKS rotation; print PEM and RFC 7638 "
"thumbprint."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Write the bare PEM to this path (mode 0600) instead of printing it to "
"stdout. The kid and rotation recipe still go to stdout."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"RSA key size in bits. Default and floor 2048 (FIPS 186-4); compliance "
"regimes targeting 128-bit security strength typically request 3072+."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Rotation recipe (overlap window prevents in-flight JWT invalidation):\n"
"  1. Move current OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY into\n"
"     OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEYS_INACTIVE.\n"
"  2. Set OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY to the PEM above.\n"
"  3. Restart Auth. JWKS now publishes both kids; existing JWTs validate.\n"
"  4. After your access-token TTL x 2, drop the old PEM from\n"
"     OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEYS_INACTIVE."
msgstr ""

