"Whitelist of Django groups allowed to authenticate this application. A user "
"is granted access if their state OR any of their groups appears in either "
"whitelist; leave both empty to open the app."
msgstr ""

msgid "Active"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Deactivated applications (``Active`` unchecked) cannot issue authorization "
"codes or tokens. Toggling this off is the operator-facing kill switch for a "
"compromised or retired client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Enables additional OIDC debug logging (INFO). Secrets/tokens are always "
"redacted/masked according to settings."
msgstr ""

msgid "PKCE required"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If enabled, this application must use PKCE on the authorization endpoint "
"(RFC 7636 / 9700). Disable only for known-incompatible clients; new "
"applications default to enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid "Access token format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Wire format of access tokens issued for this application. Leave blank to use "
"the deployment-wide default "
"(OAUTH2_PROVIDER['ALLIANCEAUTH_OIDC_DEFAULT_ACCESS_TOKEN_FORMAT'], or "
"'opaque' if unset)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Back-channel logout URI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"RP endpoint that accepts back-channel logout_token POSTs (OIDC Back-Channel "
"Logout 1.0). Leave blank to disable. https:// required unless DEBUG is on; "
"host must resolve to a public IP."
msgstr ""

msgid "Back-Channel Logout: explicit revoke only"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When checked, this RP receives a back-channel logout_token ONLY when an "
"operator runs oidc_revoke_user_tokens. Lifecycle events (deactivation, group/"
"state changes, account deletion) will NOT fan out to this RP. Default is "
"unchecked (all five triggers fire)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JWT access tokens require the application's id_token signing algorithm to be "
"RS256, not HS256. Either set Algorithm to RS256 or pick an opaque (or blank) "
"access-token format."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"NUL byte (\\x00) is not permitted in URI fields; legacy parsers truncate at "
"NUL and would mean two different things to two different consumers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"backchannel_logout_uri must use https:// unless DEBUG is enabled "
"(development only)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"backchannel_logout_uri must resolve to a public IP; private/loopback/link-"
"local/unspecified addresses are blocked. Set "
"ALLIANCEAUTH_OIDC_LOGOUT_URI_ALLOW_PRIVATE=True for dev environments."
msgstr ""

